We now apply Gauss-Jordan Elimination to transform MnM_{n} into reduced row echelon form. In particular, we seek the value of Tn=f3T_{n}=f_{3}. We will denote the reduced row echelon form of MnM_{n} as RnR_{n}.
We denote the submatrix formed by omitting the last row and column of MnM_{n} as Mn​[−1]M_{n}[-1]. Note that Mn−1M_{n-1} is very similar to Mn​[−1]M_{n}[-1]. In particular, Mn​[−1]M_{n}[-1] differs from Mn−1M_{n-1} only in the (n−1)(n-1)th column, which is negated. We proceed with the following algorithm.
We first add each row to the one beneath it, putting MnM_{n} into row echelon form.
