Remark 3.12.
Matrix 3.3 is extremely similar to the out-degree Laplacian matrix of KnK_{n}. In fact, the matrix representation of System 3.1 is exactly the out-degree Laplacian. The concept of using the out-degree Laplacian of a directed graph DD to analyze the periods of parallel chip-firing games on DD was previously mentioned by Prisner Prisner (1994), though the method of Gauss-Jordan Elimination is novel in the context of chip-firing games.
3.4 Complete Bipartite Graphs
Let τ⁡(a,b)\tau(a,\,b) be the maximum possible period of a parallel chip-firing game on an orientation of Ka,bK_{a,\,b}, with a≤ba\leq b. We show that τ⁡(a,b)\tau(a,\,b) is at least asymptotic to a!a!. We conjecture that τ⁡(a,b)\tau(a,\,b) is indeed asymptotic to a!a!.
Conjecture 3.13.
It holds that τ⁡(a,b)=Θ⁡(a!)\tau(a,\,b)=\Theta(a!).
Let the partitions of the complete bipartite graph Ka,aK_{a,\,a} be LL and RR, where |L|=|R|=a|L|=|R|=a. Let vi∈Lv_{i}\in L if i≡1(mod2)i\equiv 1\pmod{2}, and let vi∈Rv_{i}\in R otherwise. We define the following orientation of Ka,aK_{a,a} to be a useful orientation.
•
There exist edges directed from viv_{i} to vi+1v_{i+1} for each 1≤i<n1\leq i<n, and there exists an edge directed from v2​av_{2a} to v1v_{1}.
